WEBVTT

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.410
Thanks for helping, Haruo.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:21.450
Kids your age don't usually
help their moms with the groceries.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.890
Huh? I don't think that's true.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.420
You may not be able to see Akira anymore,

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:30.860
but it seems you're
relieved of a great burden.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.930
Oh, yeah...

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:39.170
If she's gonna work hard,
then I've got to, too.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.070
Haruo...

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:44.440
I mean, we've been separated
a bunch of times before.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.440
And yet, there we were,
sitting together in front of a game.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.450
If we get to see each other again,

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.920
I want to share the joy of whatever
new game is out with her.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.450
It's what I look forward to the most.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.990
I'm allowed to be positive, right?

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.960
It also sounds like
an excuse to play games.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:09.770
But, if you can't be serious about a hobby
you probably can't be about anything.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:13.040
I'll support your decision.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:16.670
Follow through with
what you believe is right.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.710
<i>Haruo, you've been coming</i>
<i>every day lately.</i>

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.150
<i>You're even more serious </i>
<i>about it than usual.</i>

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.120
<i>It's hard to believe you were </i>
<i>so troubled before the summer.</i>

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.360
Damn it! I can't beat Ryo
no matter how many times I play.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:40.830
<i>You've grown, Haruo.</i>

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.100
<i>You're a truly honorable man.</i>

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:46.270
<i>Look, Haruo.</i>
<i>Do you know why he fights?</i>

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.270
<i>Why he continues down such a hellish path?</i>

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.610
<i>Why he's braving such a dangerous journey?</i>

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:53.910
<i>Because he, too...</i>

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.410
<i>will keep moving forward</i>
<i>even if he gets pummeled.</i>

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.780
<i>Do you know why?</i>

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.880
<i>It's all for their loved ones.</i>

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.390
<i>Battles can be heartless.</i>

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.790
<i>But you can't afford to lose.</i>

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:08.990
<i>Go for it, Haruo!</i>

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.760
<i>Push forward alongside them!</i>

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.930
-You good?
-Yeah.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.440
TO HIDAKA

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.440
<i>Yaguchi...</i>

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.510
<i>I invite you to a challenge.</i>

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:13.780
<i>Long time no see. I am now </i>
<i>prepared to settle the score.</i>

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:18.050
<i>Let's do it tomorrow. If not, </i>
<i>how about the day after around noon?</i>

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.920
"I will be waiting. Haruo Yaguchi."

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.820
These words are spaced erratically.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:24.260
Nikotama.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:26.290
-Is this the guy?
-Yeah.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:30.630
Then tonight, let's work on
the final touches at my place.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.240
<i>This Felicia is really strong. </i>
<i>I don't think I can beat her.</i>

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.980
<i>I thought I'd gotten better,</i>
<i>but I still have a long way to go.</i>

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.020
I like you.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.790
You have multiple wins,

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:55.260
but you continue to practice alone
even without an opponent.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.360
I see you here everyday.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.290
U-Um...

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.130
I'm the Felicia from earlier.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.670
Your Huitzil is so polished. I love it.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.210
The way you don't use Confusioner
for your opponent's instant death,

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:12.570
shows your kindness.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.310
I hate that technique!

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.380
Whoever came up with it must be a sadist.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.180
<i>I didn't know there were other strong</i>
<i>female players besides Ono.</i>

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:26.490
By the way, do you want to be stronger?

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.490
I sense a strong tenacity in you.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.100
As if you have a battle coming up
that you can't lose.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:35.960
Take this.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.670
If you want to aim for higher, come here.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.110
GAME SHOP IGUANA

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.910
<i>What is this place?</i>

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.010
Welcome to the world of night gaming.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.110
Night gaming?

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:56.420
This is a place where those
who seek strength gather.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:01.690
This privately-run shop
hosts battles after hours.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.630
For free, of course.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.500
<i>What's with all the consecutive wins?</i>
<i>Incredible!</i>

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:13.800
Most of the people here now are the ones
with the consecutive wins.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.110
I'm Takadanobaba Sagat.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:19.340
I'm Oimachi Orbus.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:21.310
I'm Kuhombutsu Blanka.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.280
<i>Did Kuhombutsu even have an arcade?</i>

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:26.310
I'm Tamagawa Gakuen-mae Sasquatch.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.120
-Balls Samurai.
-Huh?

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.490
Call me Ulcer.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.990
<i>Why did you choose that name?</i>

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.460
Their strength is on another level.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:37.860
If you practice here,
you will definitely get stronger.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:41.000
Definitely stronger?

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.070
I'm Futako-Tamagawa Felicia.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.900
You can call me Nikotama.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.910
I'm Koharu Hidaka. Nice to meet you.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:54.140
Don't wait, don't let him throw!
There's no need to hold back.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.380
Right!

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:02.880
I made it sound like it was unfavorable
to use the Confusioner before.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:05.890
Forget that. You want to win, don't you?

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.220
Right!

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.790
<i>It's completely different </i>
<i>from the arcades in town.</i>

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.360
<i>Each battle feels so heavy,</i>
<i>it's almost scary.</i>

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:14.630
<i>But...</i>

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.370
<i>I...</i>

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.340
<i>won't give up!</i>

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:24.710
-Not bad.
-It's my turn next.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:29.280
Don't worry.

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:32.950
We've drilled you in using
the winning strategy.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.150
-There's no way you'll lose.
-Right.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.620
<i>Finally... it's time...</i>

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:41.490
THE DAY OF BATTLE

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:43.120
<i>...to get even with Yaguchi.</i>

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.830
Long time no see, Hidaka.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:49.800
Y-Yeah.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:53.640
So you're okay with
<i>Samurai Shodown II, KOF '95,</i>

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:56.140
then<i> Night Warriors: Darkstalkers' Revenge</i>
last, right?

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:57.270
Yeah.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:01.210
One battle per game,
the first to win two, wins.

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.910
Do you want the first
or second player side?

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.210
Second player.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.480
Got it.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.950
<i>Hidaka, let's try battling.</i>

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:16.730
No thanks, I like watching from behind.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:24.930
<i>I'm done watching from behind.</i>

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:28.440
<i>I want to stand next to Yaguchi.</i>

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:32.670
<i>If you win, I'll give up quietly.</i>

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:37.410
<i>But... if I win,</i><i>go out with me.</i>

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:39.750
<i>Let's have a fair fight!</i>

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.650
<i>First battle, fight!</i>

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:49.360
<i>Start cautiously. </i>
<i>One mistake can cost you.</i>

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.890
<i>Bad moves will lead to defeat.</i>

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:56.100
<i>It's just like a real sword fight.</i>

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.900
<i>I'm going to muster</i>
<i>all my feelings for Yaguchi</i>

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.870
<i>and hit him with everything I've got</i>
<i>through the screen.</i>

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:04.610
<i>I won't lose!</i>

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:07.540
That was so quick! Keep it up!

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.410
Her opponent is incredible.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.180
He matched her Quick Slash perfectly.

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.700
They both nail their combos
when they need to!

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.230
It's an even fight!

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:34.470
No. Koharu knows Genan's moves
like the back of her hand.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.370
There's no way she'll lose.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:37.810
<i>First win!</i>

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.940
Hidaka's taken the lead!

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.450
She did it!

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:48.880
<i>Good. Don't get comfortable just </i>
<i>because you won a round.</i>

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:53.390
<i>You need to play the second battle</i>
<i>as if it's your last.</i>

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.060
<i>Wonder if Haruo is here today, too.</i>

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.790
Go, Hidaka!

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:07.070
She did a Tsubame Gaeshi!
A tough technique!

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.240
Did you just see that?

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:13.680
He dodged Genan's slide with
a BC mini jump and attacked!

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:18.080
<i>Ukyo Tachibana...</i>

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:22.320
<i>knew he could never be with </i>
<i>the feudal lord's daughter Kei Odagiri.</i>

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:23.790
<i>But he loved her anyway.</i>

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:28.090
<i>Kei marries another man,</i>
<i>but Ukyo still has feelings for her.</i>

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:32.960
<i>In order to gift her the ultimate flower, </i>
<i>he heads into Hell.</i>

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.200
<i>Sounds like someone I know.</i>

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:40.540
YOU WIN!

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:43.040
<i>We have a winner!</i>

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:47.380
Complete victory.
He wasn't much competition.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:49.780
One win for Hidaka!
Let's dance for joy!

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.110
Woo!

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:56.990
<i>A win for now.</i>

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.720
<i>If I win the next game...</i>

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.560
<i>Why does something feel off?</i>

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:06.430
<i>Yaguchi has something Koharu lacks...</i>

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:08.960
<i>I sensed it watching their battle.</i>

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:11.530
<i>That was pathetic.</i>

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:14.700
<i>Haruo, you can't lose the next one.</i>

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:18.940
<i>The next match is KOF '95.</i>

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:22.180
<i>You'd better not have lost sight</i>
<i>of what you believe in!</i>

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:26.610
<i>What is your greatest strength</i>
<i>when it comes to fighting games?</i>

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:29.880
<i>Nice!</i>

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.420
Did you see his reaction?

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:39.630
He was expecting Hidaka to use
her usual all-female team.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:45.300
A surprise tactic using secret characters
is tough to counter. Impressive, Hidaka.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.670
<i>She looks unsatisfied.</i>

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:51.540
<i>Have patience, Koharu.</i>

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:53.740
<i>It's all for your victory.</i>

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.430
Whoa! So many effective special moves!

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:18.130
Air attacks, jump moves, rushes...
so many to choose from!

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:21.870
It's not an ultimate move, but it's
brutal enough to take half your life!

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.000
Incredible!

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:30.140
A Dark Barrier!

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:33.780
That ability even reflects aerial tools.
The opponent is left helpless!

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:35.480
Knock him out, Hidaka!

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:45.090
One more to go!

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:49.530
<i>Haruo! Takuma and Robert are out, </i>
<i>only Ryo is left!</i>

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:50.830
<i>Will you be okay?</i>

00:12:57.970 --> 00:12:59.170
Rugal!

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:02.780
But she still has Saisyu and Heidern left!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.110
-You can do it!
<i>-No...</i>

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:06.210
<i>it's one thing if she's Rugal,</i>
<i>whose technical abilities alone</i>

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:07.250
<i>can support him.</i>

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.080
<i>But against the Invincible Dragon Ryo,</i>

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.490
<i>Saisyu and Heidern are just thin veneers.</i>

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:21.830
<i>And it just became clear to me</i>

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:24.570
<i>what it is that Yaguchi has</i>
<i>that Koharu doesn't.</i>

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:27.670
<i>While she is determined to win,</i>

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:30.840
<i>he is enjoying himself while fighting.</i>

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.420
-One to one...
-They're even now.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.880
<i>I relied too much</i>
<i>on using strong characters.</i>

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:46.550
<i>I should've used two of my</i>
<i>usual characters with Rugal.</i>

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.400
<i>I was too hasty to win!</i>

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.100
W-What a guy.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:07.580
He outdid those strong characters
using only Ryo Sakazaki!

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:11.110
<i>Haruo...</i>

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.150
<i>One win, one loss.</i>

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:18.350
<i>All that's left is</i>
<i>Night Warriors: Darkstalkers' Revenge!</i>

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:19.920
<i>The final match!</i>

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:34.940
So you came?

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.110
I'm sure there's a lot
I don't know about...

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:39.510
but I'll be watching over you.

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:40.410
Thanks.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.380
Do your best, Hidaka!

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:44.450
Yes, we are on your side.

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:46.710
<i>One win and one loss...</i>

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:48.850
Just relax, Koharu.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:52.990
Remember to play like you usually do.

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.590
I know you'll be okay.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:57.130
Nikotama...

00:14:58.190 --> 00:15:00.400
In critical moments,

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:03.430
it's common to lose the control
of the lever.

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:07.000
Be conscious of the commands
you're inputting.

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:08.370
Right!

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.540
<i>I used to think games were just games.</i>

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:14.380
<i>I never thought it'd turn into </i>
<i>such a serious battle.</i>

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:15.580
<i>Yaguchi...</i>

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:19.110
<i>One more battle to decide the match.</i>

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.380
<i>I feel surprisingly calm.</i>

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:24.120
<i>I just have to play like I always do.</i>

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.260
Koharu,

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:33.060
use everything you've learned
from night gaming, right here and now.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:35.760
<i>Please accept it, Yaguchi,</i>

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.270
<i>my feelings for you!</i>

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.600
H-He used a Low Slash from the start!

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:45.270
He's closing in!

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:47.510
Bishamon is really
putting the pressure on!

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:50.680
<i>Huitzil is a long-range fighter,</i>

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:53.050
<i>so when the close-range fighter Bishamon</i>
<i>gets too close,</i>

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:54.420
<i>the situation gets sticky.</i>

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.020
<i>She needs to keep her distance.</i>

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.990
What a nasty combo attack!

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.960
She's fine, she's guarding well!

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:10.300
It's like a woman
rejecting a persistent man!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:13.130
<i>I'm the persistent one...</i>

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:15.940
<i>and Yaguchi's the one </i>
<i>who is rejecting!</i>

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:20.840
She has cornered him with
a guard-cancel reflect chain!

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:22.310
She has him cornered!

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:24.980
<i>Oh no!</i>

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:30.820
<i>You need to watch out for </i>
<i>Bishamon's Oni Kubi Hineri.</i>

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:34.020
<i>But that's completely different </i>
<i>from a throw technique.</i>

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:36.390
<i>That guy is amazing.</i>

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:43.870
Ugh, he won!

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:45.800
<i>Both of them are incredible!</i>

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:51.840
<i>Huitzil can't compete to Bishamon </i>
<i>when it comes to speed.</i>

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:54.910
<i>I'll compensate using technique!</i>

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:57.810
Clean hit.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.020
<i>I have to win!</i>

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.950
<i>I'll beat Yaguchi, the guy I love...</i>

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:06.490
<i>so we can play games together,</i>
<i>go on dates together...</i>

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:09.420
<i>and do all the things couples do!</i>

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:16.160
Unbelievable!
It's a demonic instant death combo!

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:18.370
<i>That's right, Koharu.</i>

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:21.070
<i>There's nothing wrong with relying </i>
<i>on the Confusioner.</i>

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:23.140
<i>It's a method to win.</i>

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.840
<i>What a scary special move.</i>

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.110
<i>Will you be okay, Haruo?</i>

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:33.210
<i>Haruo. You can't afford to lose</i>
<i>this master-versus-pupil match.</i>

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:37.120
<i>She has certainly trained harder, </i>

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:41.090
<i>but I know you worked your butt off.</i>

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:47.400
<i>I've watched you.</i>

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:51.000
<i>You worked day and night,</i>

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:54.500
<i>and gave more than half of </i>
<i>your earnings to your family.</i>

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.340
<i>You were frugal with </i>
<i>your remaining earnings,</i>

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:01.310
<i>and deliberately went to arcades</i>
<i>further away 'cause it was cheaper.</i>

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:02.810
<i>And...</i>

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:06.480
<i>you took notes on whatever you couldn't </i>
<i>do in a match that day,</i>

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:09.320
<i>studied them and used them</i>
<i>to achieve your next goal.</i>

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.620
<i>I've witnessed your countless efforts.</i>

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:14.660
<i>Got him!</i>

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:16.860
<i>I've watched you through all of it!</i>

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:23.400
He made up for the instant death combo
with consecutive mid-range kicks!

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:29.100
<i>Relax. Small moves, Koharu.</i>

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:32.140
<i>Small moves and use the Confusioner again.</i>

00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:39.980
<i>Geez, she's got crazy reflexes.</i>

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:43.180
<i>She guard-cancels everything I do.</i>

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:46.390
<i>Haruo...</i>

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:50.290
<i>are you seeing her glimpses?</i>

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.080
How's that, Hidaka?

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.650
Did you see my skills?

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.920
You've learned some awesome moves!

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:21.660
My hands won't stop trembling.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.990
I almost puked from
fear of the Confusioner!

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:27.190
Your skills were fierce,

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:29.930
but I had to overcome them
to move forward!

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.970
Thanks to you, the comeback
of the godly Yaguchi--

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:35.500
You must be an idiot!

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:37.940
Who cares about the "comeback
of the godly Yaguchi"?

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:40.910
This was a match between you and me!

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:42.010
You piss me off!

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:43.980
You have no idea how I feel!

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:48.180
By "forward" you mean to Ono, right?

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:49.620
Stop that, Hidaka!

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.590
What was that storm of Guard Cancels?

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:53.950
You were toying with me!

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:55.460
Do you think I'm stupid?

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:56.460
I wasn't--

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:59.190
You deliberately chose not
to use Oni Kubi Hineri.

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:00.900
Out of pity or something?

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:02.430
I tried to do it...

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:04.230
-Ow!
-No!

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:08.000
I'm not gonna let you say you beat me
until you beat me two more times!

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:09.170
W-What?

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:12.870
I won two out of three before!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.640
What?! Hidaka, you--

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:16.940
Damn it! You're so damn loved!

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:20.010
Let's chop up this Yaguchi guy
and turn him into sashimi!

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:21.220
Wait!

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.490
Are you all right, Koharu?

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:28.260
No, I'm so angry!

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:30.620
Towards Yaguchi too, but...

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:35.800
I'm angry at myself.
I practiced so much, but I still lost.

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:42.240
That anger is proof
that you truly love gaming.

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:45.910
Koharu, if you use that
love and anger as fuel...

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:49.440
it'll only make you stronger.

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:57.850
<i>He's not cool at all,</i>

00:20:58.320 --> 00:20:59.720
<i>he's totally oblivious,</i>

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:02.090
<i>and I never know what he's thinking...</i>

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:06.460
<i>but I still fell for him. What can I do?</i>

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:09.700
<i>I don't want to give up on Yaguchi</i>
<i>or on fighting games.</i>

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:13.170
<i>I'm going to use this to become stronger!</i>

00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:51.930
Subtitle translation by Emily Noguchi

00:22:52.030 --> 00:22:54.440
ISLAND

00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:59.610
<i>DonPachi!</i><i>There are so many bullets!</i>

00:22:59.740 --> 00:23:01.940
<i>Gotta take my hat off </i>
<i>to this manic shoot 'em up.</i>

00:23:02.740 --> 00:23:05.210
<i>Concentrate on dodging the bullets...</i>

00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:09.420
Your score goes way up depending on
the number of bombs you have left.

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:12.020
<i>Try your best not to use the bombs.</i>

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:18.690
<i>As always, I don't have </i>
<i>any talent for shooting games.</i>

00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:22.860
<i>Man, there are so many new games out.</i>

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:25.870
<i>But not being able </i>
<i>to play them with Ono...</i>

00:23:26.700 --> 00:23:28.070
<i>makes me feel sad.</i>

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:33.040
<i>That back looks familiar...</i>

00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:34.280
<i>It can't be!</i>

00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:37.480
<i>She can't be playing strip Mahjong...</i>

00:23:38.650 --> 00:23:39.610
Ono!

00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:47.120
Damn it! I accidentally
did a <i>chi </i>thanks to you.

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:48.660
Oh, um, sorry.

00:23:48.890 --> 00:23:51.060
Oh, well. Haruo Yaguchi.

00:23:51.290 --> 00:23:53.360
You look just as stupid
as in that <i>purikura</i> pic.

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:54.730
How do you know about that?

00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:59.470
Well, it's because
I'm Akira's elder sister of course.

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:02.300
What? Ono's sister?

00:24:10.840 --> 00:24:14.650
<i>The feeling in the air when the game you </i>
<i>wanted to play gets installed is amazing!</i>

00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:16.580
<i>The crowd that surrounds the machine,</i>

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:18.620
<i>the players taking turns after each match!</i>

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:20.750
<i>Every time a new character is chosen,</i>

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:22.860
<i>every time a new technique is used,</i>

00:24:22.990 --> 00:24:24.460
<i>the crowd goes wild!</i>
